Track 3: Do the Stars Remember?
- Story & Context: Years later, perched on a forgotten rooftop observatory overlooking the city, Kael found an old, dust-coated telescope pointed vaguely towards the heavens, its lens reflecting the distant glow of the now-legendary underground club. The subtle scent of damp concrete and residual electricity still clung to his clothes from the night before, a constant reminder of the 'flux-burners' who continued to seek transcendence there, a place where Lyra's spirit was said to still dance among the projected galaxies. "Every shattered light, a promise kept in the dark," he sang softly, remembering the profound shifts that began in that subatomic crucible.
